article_content:
Mae hyfforddwr tîm rygbi dan-20 Cymru wedi cael ei orfodi i newid ei dîm yn hwyr oherwydd anaf.

Bydd Cymru yn herio De Affrica ym Mhencampwriaeth Ifanc y Byd yn y Stade de la Rabine, Vannes, Ffrainc yn ddiweddarach, a hynny yn y rownd gynderfynol.

Mae'r clo Carwyn Jones wedi cael anaf wrth ymarfer, ac mae Jack Jones yn cymryd ei le gyda James Benjamin yn llenwi'r bwlch ar y fainc.

Fe gurodd Cymru dan-20 Ariannin dan-20 o 25-20 i orffen ar frig grŵp C yn y gystadleiaeth ddydd Iau diwethaf.

Aeth Cymru i'r rownd gynderfynol y tymor diwethaf hefyd, ond mae'r hyfforddwr Danny Wilson yn benderfynnol o fynd un cam yn well y tro hwn.

"Rydym wedi cael golwg go dda ar Dde Affrica erbyn hyn," meddai Wilson, ac fe fydd gan ein pac lawer iawn o waith i wneud ddydd Mawrth.

"Maen nhw'n debyg i'r tîm llawn, sef pac trwm, ond mae ganddyn nhw hefyd dri o'r olwyr sy'n beryglus iawn ac fe fydd rhaid i ni fod yn wyliadwrus.

"Rydym yn falch o gyrraedd y nod a osodon ni i ni'n hunain ar y dechrau, sef cyrraedd y pedwar olaf, ond dydyn ni ddim wedi gorffen eto."

15. Jordan Williams (Scarlets / Llanelli);
14. Ashley Evans (Gweilch/ Pen-y-bont);
13. Steffan Hughes (Scarlets / Llanelli);
9. Rhodri Williams (Scarlets/ Llanymddyfri);
1. Gareth Thomas (Scarlets/ Cwins Caerfyrddin);
6. Sion Bennett (Scarlets/ Caerfyrddin);
7. Ellis Jenkins (goleuddydd, Gleision/Caerdydd);
Eilyddion: Elliot Dee (Dreigiau/Bedwas), Thomas Davies (Gleision/Caerdydd), Dan Suter (Gweilch/Pen-y-bont), James Benjamin (Dreigiau/Bedwas), Daniel Thomas (Scarlets/ Llanelli), Joshua Davies (Dreigiau/Bedwas), Aaron Warren (Llanymddyfri), Thomas Pascoe (Gleision/Pontypridd).

translated_content:
The Wales Under-20 rugby team coach has been forced to make a late team change due to an injury.

Wales will face South Africa in the World Youth Championship at the Stade de la Rabine in Vannes, France, in the decisive round.

Captain Carwyn Jones suffered an injury during training, with Jack Jones taking his place and James Benjamin filling the gap on the bench.

Wales' Under-20 team defeated Andorra Under-20 25-20 to finish third in Group C last Thursday.

Wales reached the decisive round last year too, but coach Danny Wilson is determined to go one step further this time.

'We've had a good look at South Africa so far,' said Wilson, and our pack has a lot of work to do on Monday.

'They resemble the senior team, a heavy pack, but they also have three dangerous forwards, and we must remain vigilant.

'We are proud to achieve the goal and set ourselves the initial target of reaching the top four, but we haven't finished yet.'

15. Jordan Williams (Scarlets/Llanelli);
14. Ashley Evans (Dragons/Newport);
13. Steffan Hughes (Scarlets/Llanelli);
9. Rhodri Williams (Scarlets/Carmarthen);
1. Gareth Thomas (Scarlets/Cardiff Castle);
6. Sion Bennett (Scarlets/Cardiff);
7. Ellis Jenkins (captain, Blues/Cardiff);
Replacements: Elliot Dee (Dragons/Bedwas), Thomas Davies (Blues/Cardiff), Dan Suter (Dragons/Newport), James Benjamin (Dragons/Bedwas), Daniel Thomas (Scarlets/Llanelli), Joshua Davies (Dragons/Bedwas), Aaron Warren (Carmarthen), Thomas Pascoe (Blues/Pontypridd).
